y check (opening balance vs. prior closing balance) but lacked prior-statement data. This should not mark the field as incorrect; instead, it should be treated as \"not cross-validated\" while still accepting the value if it matches the current document.\n\nUnderlying pattern of mistakes:\n- Meta fields (like `transaction_count` and `confidence_level`) are not being derived from or aligned with the actual parsed content and validation results.\n- Cross-statement validation is being reported as an error rather than as a non-blocking informational note when prerequisite data (previous statement) is missing.\n\nThese issues are systemic: they can recur whenever transaction counts are inferred rather than computed, confidence is left at a default value, or cross-period checks are attempted without prior data. The correction rules must therefore focus on (a) deriving counts from actual arrays, (b) computing confidence from validation outcomes, and (c) treating missing cross-period data as a non-error condition.",
